@startuml use-cases
' Use-case diagram - Smart Campus study room booking (revised from the assistant's draft,
' see lab-report.md sections 6-7). Two actors outside the boundary, six use cases inside.

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus study room booking" {
  usecase "View availability"      as UC01
  usecase "Book room"              as UC02
  usecase "Cancel booking"         as UC03
  usecase "Block or unblock room"  as UC04
  usecase "Review usage"           as UC05
  usecase "Send confirmation"      as UC06

  ' why: UC-06 says the system confirms every successful booking - it is a mandatory part of Book room, not an option
  UC02 ..> UC06 : <<include>>
  ' why: UC-06 also confirms every successful cancellation
  UC03 ..> UC06 : <<include>>
}

' Student triggers these three (US-01, US-02, US-03)
Student -- UC01
Student -- UC02
Student -- UC03

' Administrator triggers these two (US-05, US-06, US-07)
UC04 -- Administrator
UC05 -- Administrator

' No actor triggers Send confirmation: the system performs it inside UC-02 / UC-03 (US-04)

note bottom of UC02
  R1 start in the future (start = now is rejected)
  R2 at most two hours (exactly 2 h is allowed)
  R3 no overlap for the same room
     (ending when another begins is allowed)
  R4 blocked room cannot be booked
end note
@enduml
